---
import { DiaTextReveal } from '../sora-ui/texts/dia-text-reveal';
import { SoraCtaButton } from '../sora-ui/SoraCtaButton';

const revealColors = ['#4d7cff', '#38bdf8', '#a5b4fc', '#e1e1fe'];
---

<section class="hero-section" id="mission">
  <div class="content-column">
    <div class="hero-header-super">
      <h1 class="hero-title">
        Building the infrastructure for the{' '}
        <DiaTextReveal
          client:load
          className="hero-dia-reveal"
          text={['agentic era.', 'agentic economy.', 'age of agents.']}
          colors={revealColors}
          duration={1.4}
          holdDuration={2.2}
          repeat
          fixedWidth
        />
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Software is learning to act. Agents now write code, transact, negotiate,
        and coordinate on behalf of people and institutions, faster than the
        infrastructure beneath them can adapt. We are building the foundations
        they need: safe, clean, and governable from the first layer.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-banner-container tick-box">
      <img
        src="/images/kalaris-hero-banner.png"
        alt="Kalaris Labs"
        width="1024"
        height="173"
        class="hero-banner-image"
        loading="eager"
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="manifesto-stream">
      <p>
        The agentic era needs its own{' '}
        <a href="/manifesto" class="source-backlink">
          harnesses, protocols, and markets<span
            class="backlink-icon"
            aria-hidden="true">↗</span
          >
        </a>: infrastructure that lets agents keep learning from their own work,
        communicate with one another, and act under mandates they cannot
        rewrite. Every earlier era of computing got its infrastructure after the
        damage was done. This one has to be built before.
      </p>

      <p class="manifesto-callout">
        <a href="/manifesto" class="source-backlink callout-link">
          <DiaTextReveal
            client:visible
            text="The rules have to exist before the actors do."
            colors={revealColors}
            duration={1.6}
          /><span class="backlink-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </p>

      <p>
        Scaling pre-training and post-training will keep making models more
        capable. It will not, on its own, make them accountable. An agent that
        is capable but ungoverned is not progress; it is a liability with a
        network connection.
      </p>

      <p>
        We study how agents behave when they share a world, through{' '}
        <a href="/blog/simulating-society" class="source-backlink">
          multi-agent simulation<span class="backlink-icon" aria-hidden="true"
            >↗</span
          >
        </a>, game theory, and the{' '}
        <a href="/blog/machine-payable-web" class="source-backlink">
          economics of the agentic economy<span
            class="backlink-icon"
            aria-hidden="true">↗</span
          >
        </a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        And we measure honestly: evaluations that are{' '}
        <a href="/blog/specification-gaming" class="source-backlink">
          hard to game<span class="backlink-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>, with alignment, safety, and security as design constraints on
        everything we build.
      </p>

      <div class="hero-actions">
        <SoraCtaButton client:load href="/manifesto">
          Read the manifesto →
        </SoraCtaButton>
        <a class="button button-secondary" href="/research">
          Explore research <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
